  "question": {
    "text": "If the four distinct points $(4,6),(-1,5),(0,0)$ and $(\\mathrm{k}, 3 \\mathrm{k})$ lie on a circle of radius r , then $10 \\mathrm{k}+\\mathrm{r}^2$ is equal to",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "Du0r2",
      "text": "$32$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HdhCa",
      "text": "$33$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "9mhY5",
      "text": "$34$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "Vaz9S",
      "text": "$35$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/w5QF5q3WSX9TVVZWDnYvDD8cYtwnKdVrF-1HUrSr7QU.original.fullsize.png\"/><br/>$\\mathrm{m}_1 \\mathrm{~m}_2=-1$ so right angle equation circle is<br/>$\\begin{aligned}<br/>& (x-4)(x-0)+(y-6)(y-0)=0 \\\\\n& x^2+y^2-4 x-6 y=0<br/>\\end{aligned}$<br/>$(\\mathrm{k}, 3 \\mathrm{k})$ lies on it so<br/>$\\begin{aligned}<br/>& \\mathrm{k}^2+9 \\mathrm{k}^2-4 \\mathrm{k}-18 \\mathrm{k}=0 \\\\\n& 10 \\mathrm{k}^2-22 \\mathrm{k}=0<br/>\\end{aligned}$<br/>$\\mathrm{k}=0, \\frac{11}{5}$<br/>$\\mathrm{k}=0$ is not possible so $\\mathrm{k}=\\frac{11}{5}$<br/>also $\\mathrm{r}=\\sqrt{4+9}=\\sqrt{13}$<br/>so $10 \\mathrm{k}+\\mathrm{r}^2=10 \\cdot \\frac{11}{5}+(\\sqrt{13})^2=35$",
    "image": null
  },
